---
layout: base.njk
---
{#
  Layout for input_custom_post/ — hand-written HTML block posts.

  Sits between base.njk and a raw body fragment. base.njk supplies <!DOCTYPE>,
  the <head>, nav.njk and footer.njk; this file adds the furniture every notebook
  post carries — the date, the <h1>, and the back links — so a hand-author writes
  the BODY ONLY and still gets a page that matches the rest of the Notebook.

  WHY THIS IS NOT post.njk
  post.njk wraps everything in `.post-container > .prose`, which is correct for
  markdown and wrong for blocks: a full-bleed hero cannot escape a max-width
  column. Here {{ content }} is emitted at FULL WIDTH and each block brings its
  own container. That is the one real difference; the header and footer blocks
  below are copied from post.njk deliberately so the two page kinds look
  identical. Change one, change the other.

  A third copy of that header block lives in the page builder, at
  page_builder_app_v2/src/puck/components/Hero.tsx (staticHeader). Builder pages
  go to input_build_page/ and use base.njk directly, so they emit it themselves.
  If those pages ever move to this layout, delete staticHeader rather than
  keeping two.

  FRONT MATTER THIS LAYOUT READS
    header: false   omit the date/title/back-link block entirely, for a page
                    that opens on its own hero and carries its own title.
    outline: true   add the "On this page" panel, built from the h2/h3 in the
                    body. Off by default: addAnchors rewrites every heading in
                    the fragment, including ones inside a hero, which is rarely
                    what a block page wants.
  Everything else (title, date, tags, image, description, navScroll,
  customJsonLd) is read by base.njk, not here.
#}

{% if outline %}
{% set body = content | addAnchors %}
{% set toclist = body | toc %}
{% else %}
{% set body = content %}
{% set toclist = "" %}
{% endif %}

{% if toclist %}
{# No-JS article outline: hidden checkbox drives the toggle. Same markup as post.njk. #}
<input type="checkbox" id="article-outline-toggle" class="article-outline-toggle">
<aside class="article-outline-panel">
    <p class="article-outline-heading">On this page</p>
    {{ toclist | safe }}
</aside>
<label for="article-outline-toggle" class="article-outline-btn" title="Toggle outline" aria-label="Toggle outline">
    <span class="article-outline-icon-open" aria-hidden="true">E</span>
    <span class="article-outline-icon-close" aria-hidden="true">X</span>
</label>
{% endif %}

{% if header != false %}
{# Date, title, then the back link — the link sits UNDER the title so the first
   thing on the page is the page's own name. Identical to post.njk. #}
<div class="post-container pt-24 extra_fade_effect">
    <div class="mb-8 pb-8 border-b border-neutral-200 dark:border-neutral-800">
        <time class="text-sm font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-wider" datetime="{{ date | isoStamp }}">
            {{ date | readableDate }}
        </time>
        <h1 class="text-5xl md:text-6xl text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mt-4 mb-4 uppercase tracking-wider">
            {{ title }}
        </h1>
        <a href="/notebook.html" class="inline-flex items-center text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 hover:text-neutral-900 dark:hover:text-white transition-colors font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">
           ← Back to Notebook
        </a>
    </div>
</div>
{% endif %}

{# FULL WIDTH on purpose — see the note at the top. Each block supplies its own
   container: .post-container for a text column, nothing for a full-bleed one. #}
{{ body | safe }}

<div class="post-container pt-24">
  <hr>
  <div class="py-2">
    <time class="text-sm font-mono text-neutral-500 dark:text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-wider" datetime="{{ date | isoStamp }}">
        {{ date | readableDate }}
    </time>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="post-container pt-6 pb-12">
    <a href="/notebook.html" class="inline-block border-b-2 border-black dark:border-white pb-1 hover:opacity-50 transition text-lg tracking-widest">
      ← NOTEBOOK FRONT PAGE
    </a>
</div>
